---
export const title = 'Read-only and states';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  <code>readonly</code> turns the rating into a display, such as a product's average review: any
  value is drawn, with a partly filled star, and it is one image named "Rated 4.3 out of 5" that is
  not in the tab order.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-rating readonly value='4.3'></wc-rating>
</DemoComponentCard>

<p>
  The rating is form-associated: inside a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> the score is submitted under
  <code>name</code>, no score submits nothing, <code>required</code> blocks submission until one is
  picked, and <code>form.reset()</code> restores the first value.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;'>
    <wc-rating label='Required' required helper-text='Pick at least one star'></wc-rating>
    <wc-rating label='Error' error error-text='Rate the delivery too' value='2'></wc-rating>
    <wc-rating label='Disabled' disabled value='3'></wc-rating>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>
